<edge source="russia_ukraine_warfare::political_will_arms" target="alliance_munitions_strai::contingency_planning" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained political commitments to supply arms compel defense planners to develop and formalize logistics, staging, training and decision rules to manage deliveries and sustainment.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_warfare</data>
  <data key="d39">alliance_munitions_strai</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_warfare::political_will_arms" target="currency_activism::gov_bond_yields" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained external political commitment to large arms transfers translates into higher expected fiscal outlays, guarantees and contingent liabilities for supplier governments, increasing sovereign borrowing needs and term premia and lifting bond yields.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_warfare</data>
  <data key="d39">currency_activism</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_warfare::political_will_arms" target="iran_hormuz_standoff::military_coercion_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased political will to supply weapons driven by Russia‑Ukraine fighting accelerates deliveries of naval/anti-ship systems and training to regional partners, enabling more frequent and capable coercive deployments in the Strait of Hormuz.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_warfare</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
