  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">A sharp uptick in attacks, mines, or interdictions raises insurers' and states' threat assessments, prompting coastal states, navies or coalition task forces to institute exclusion zones, convoy requirements, or port restrictions that actively restrict or regulate commercial movement.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
