<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="alliance_munitions_strai::alliance_cohesion" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">When the U.S. tightens export controls on AI‑relevant hardware and tools, like advanced semiconductors and development software, allied governments coordinate lists, licensing rules and joint enforcement to avoid loopholes, increasing policy and operational alignment among partners.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">alliance_munitions_strai</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="currency_activism::crossborder_capital_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter export controls raise compliance costs, bar transactions and trigger forced divestments and deal cancellations between jurisdictions, causing investors and firms to halt or reroute cross‑border investments and thus reducing net cross‑border capital flows.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">currency_activism</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="currency_activism::gov_bond_yields" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Intensified export restrictions that materially impair a targeted country’s tech export earnings and investment outlook increase sovereign growth and credit‑risk premia, directly lifting government bond yields as investors price higher term premia and default risk.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">currency_activism</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="iran_hormuz_standoff::energy_export_volume" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter US/Western export controls on China drive Beijing to secure alternative, discounted energy supplies (including increased crude purchases from Iran) to insulate its economy, raising the volume of Iranian exports moving through or from the Gulf.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
