<edge source="currency_activism::exchange_rate_level" target="alliance_munitions_strai::alliance_cohesion" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A rapid depreciation of an allied state's currency forces its government to divert budgetary resources to currency support and social stabilizers, producing domestic pressure to cut or delay allied contributions and generating disputes over burden‑sharing that reduce cohesion.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">currency_activism</data>
  <data key="d39">alliance_munitions_strai</data>
</edge>
<edge source="currency_activism::exchange_rate_level" target="russia_ukraine_warfare::interceptor_use_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">A weaker Russian ruble (a higher exchange-rate reading) raises the domestic cost of imported missiles, guidance systems and fuel, which tends to reduce Russian long‑range strike tempo and thus lowers the rate at which Ukrainian air‑defence interceptors are consumed.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">currency_activism</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_warfare</data>
</edge>
