<edge source="currency_activism::crossborder_capital_flow" target="alliance_munitions_strai::contingency_planning" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in freely available cross‑border capital reduces the need for pre‑financing and large prepositioned stockpiles, so planners scale back contingency prepositioning and detailed short‑term logistics plans (conversely, a sudden tightening prompts expanded contingency planning).</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">currency_activism</data>
  <data key="d39">alliance_munitions_strai</data>
</edge>
<edge source="currency_activism::crossborder_capital_flow" target="iran_hormuz_standoff::energy_export_volume" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.62</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in cross-border capital flows (easier inflows of hard currency and trade finance) directly enables timely payment and settlement for hydrocarbon buyers and logistics providers, increasing the quantity of oil and gas cargoes shipped through Hormuz within weeks.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">currency_activism</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="currency_activism::crossborder_capital_flow" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::ai_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.88</data>
  <data key="d36">Increases in gross and net cross‑border capital into a country’s tech sector provide direct funding that accelerates VC deals, corporate capex and startup formation, raising the rate of AI-directed investment.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">currency_activism</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="currency_activism::crossborder_capital_flow" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained surges of foreign capital into rival-country tech sectors trigger political and national‑security concerns that prompt authorities to expand or tighten export/trade restrictions targeting technology flows.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">currency_activism</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
