<edge source="alliance_munitions_strai::escalation_risk" target="currency_activism::gov_bond_yields" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in escalation risk raises perceived sovereign credit and term premia for governments in the conflict or spillover region, driving up their government bond yields as investors demand higher compensation and domestic fiscal costs rise.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">alliance_munitions_strai</data>
  <data key="d39">currency_activism</data>
</edge>
<edge source="alliance_munitions_strai::escalation_risk" target="iran_hormuz_standoff::maritime_security_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">A higher systemic probability of escalation raises the likelihood that state or proxy actors will undertake hostile acts at sea (harassment, interdiction, mining), directly raising measured and perceived maritime security risk.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">alliance_munitions_strai</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="alliance_munitions_strai::escalation_risk" target="russia_ukraine_warfare::political_will_arms" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising systemic risk of escalation prompts caution among external governments, producing explicit limits or pauses on transfers of longer‑range or higher‑lethality systems to avoid perceived steps that could broaden the conflict.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">alliance_munitions_strai</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_warfare</data>
</edge>
<edge source="alliance_munitions_strai::escalation_risk" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::ai_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A perceptible rise in the risk of military or crisis escalation with China induces governments to reallocate budgetary resources to defense‑relevant AI and prompts private investors to channel capital into AI firms viewed as strategic, boosting AI investment flows.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">alliance_munitions_strai</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
