<edge source="alliance_munitions_strai::maritime_access_control" target="currency_activism::crossborder_capital_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Tightened maritime access controls (closures, interdictions or convoying) immediately raise shipping costs, delay cargo and trade‑finance settlements and force rerouting, which contracts trade‑related cross‑border payments and prompts investors and banks to pull back from exposed corridors.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">alliance_munitions_strai</data>
  <data key="d39">currency_activism</data>
</edge>
<edge source="alliance_munitions_strai::maritime_access_control" target="iran_hormuz_standoff::shipping_route_control" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">When allied actors increase active regulation (exclusion zones, convoying, interdiction patrols or port denial), they immediately change who can enforce and direct commercial trajectories, raising the effective control over shipping routes.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">alliance_munitions_strai</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="alliance_munitions_strai::maritime_access_control" target="russia_ukraine_warfare::interceptor_use_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained allied denial or tighter regulation of sea routes reduces or delays maritime resupply of long‑range strike munitions, lowering the volume of sea‑launched/transported missile attacks and thus the rate at which air‑defence interceptors are expended.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">alliance_munitions_strai</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_warfare</data>
</edge>
<edge source="alliance_munitions_strai::maritime_access_control" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::hardware_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Expansion of maritime access controls or interdictions disrupts seaborne shipments of specialized chips and manufacturing equipment, producing immediate bottlenecks that reduce AI hardware production and data‑center buildout throughput.</data>
